WEBVTT

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:11.970
Why?

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.860
Why has it turned to this?

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.060
Why?

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.830
Chapter 10

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.830
Evening of 
the Blizzard

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.260
It seems wide enough for a tank to get through.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.390
I guess this recon was worth it.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.890
Yep. Let's quickly get back to the squad.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.640
What's wrong? Let's hurry back to...

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.650
Wait, it's going to be difficult.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:46.650
Heh?

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.230
A blizzard is coming.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.570
In this weather? You're kidding.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.360
We need to find shelter.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:58.570
We can't get through the storm with this equipment, and traveling blindly will get us stranded.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.990
It looks like there is a cabin over there.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:01.870
Let's hurry.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.750
Hey!

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.290
Wait a minute!

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.930
Wow, it's so dusty.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.430
It looks like it hasn't been used in a while,

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:26.310
but with a cabin as good as this, we should be able to get past the blizzard just fine.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:32.020
Hey Welkin, knowing you, there is probably a good reason,

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.490
but is there really going to be a blizzard?

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.570
There should be, but why?

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.990
I thought that you might be trying to get off work.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.660
Come on, it is this sunny outside and...

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.580
Huh?

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.620
See?

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.220
Spring storm, huh?

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.510
It is a mountainous terrain.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:02.050
It isn't strange for it to snow even in this season.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.770
It was good that I was with you.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:05.350
Eh?

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.980
Well, if I were with someone else, I would be in the middle of that blizzard, right?

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:16.280
If you say that, I guess there was some good in coming along with you.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.200
How long do we have to stay like this?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.530
That depends on the weather.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.160
Everyone is probably worried.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.080
Hmm?

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.710
I'll go and see if there are any blankets in the back.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.090
Thanks.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.560
Are you okay?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.680
Oh, I'm fine.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.480
I may not look it, but I am pretty strong against the chill.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.660
Ah, it's okay. That's yours.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.080
What are you talking about, freezing like that?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.460
I'm the commander, and I have a duty to protect my...

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.710
It's okay. If we put it like this...

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.050
the two of us can use the blanket together, right?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.770
Well, say something.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:31.310
Huh?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.530
I thought if we talked, we might be able to ease up a little.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.360
Even if you say so...

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.820
Anything is fine.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.120
It could be about Squad 7.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.830
It could be about this war, and...

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.540
it could be about you as well.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.670
Right.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.170
How about the habits of dungroller?

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.510
Tell me something that I would understand.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.630
Then how about where crinkle clams goes on a rainy...

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.590
Not interested.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.680
Then how about why herding nudibranches become lonely...

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.680
Please, just stop.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.560
They are good stories, you know...

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.690
Geez, why are you always like that?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:22.990
Most likely, it was Father's influence that made me interested in nature.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.530
Hm? General Gunther's?

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.330
Yeah. When we had free time, we went to a lot of places.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.660
We caught bugs in mountains, swam in rivers and stuff.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.880
A general collecting insects...

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.630
It feels a little out of place.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.420
Probably because his image as a soldier is strong.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.880
I'm sorry.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.720
You didn't want to talk about your father.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.640
It's okay.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.350
No matter how hard I try, I am "General Gunther's son."

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.640
I can't do anything about being compared to him.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.520
Being a son of a famous figure is tough, eh?

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.770
But I think it's better than having none.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:00.690
Eh?

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.990
I used to be an orphan.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:11.120
So when I came of age, there was no family around me.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.710
I'm envious that you have a memory of a family.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.420
I'm sorry.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.000
No, no. It's fine.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.170
I am sorry. I made things a little grave.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.300
But, what is family?

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.310
I do not know, either.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.100
My family was pretty complicated too.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.440
Father was always in thought as well.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.780
Even though he was praised as a hero by those around him, he wasn't able to protect my mother.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.570
My mother died amidst a battle.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:52.700
My father wasn't even there, but he said it was his fault.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:59.290
In order to keep more people from having sad thoughts,

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.460
we need to end this war as quickly as we can.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.170
Yes, that's right.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.840
Can I ask you something?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.010
What is it?

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.430
About that scarf.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.020
It stands out in the field, so I was curious.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.640
Oh this?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.900
I used to apprentice in a bakery.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:29.240
On the first day, the master looked at my face and got angry.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:34.330
"You think you can knead a bread dough when you're wavin' your long hair like that?" he said.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:38.960
So I panicked and quickly bought this, and ever since, I've always had it on.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.830
I guess you could call it my trademark.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.250
So that's what it is.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:52.430
I don't want to forget that I am a baker before I am a Militia, so this is proof of that.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.260
I say that is great.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:55.970
Huh?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.390
It sounds wonderful, I think.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.650
Thanks.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.120
Hey, Welkin.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.180
Well, let's get some rest.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:34.300
Saving up our strength is part of our duty.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.720
Good night, Alicia.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.120
Alicia.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:00.700
Alicia.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.290
Someth...

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.000
Shh. Quiet.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.680
What? What is it?

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.300
Shh.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.910
Do not resist!

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.450
If you shoot me, you'll die too.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.120
Can't you see this?

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.500
The safety pin has been removed.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.870
If it leaves my hand, it will explode.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.710
Throw down your guns!

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.340
We can't do that.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.090
We aren't going to go without a fight.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.180
What?!

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.760
Don't you see...

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.560
There is no guarantee that the grenade will blow both of us up,

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:07.270
but if we put these guns down, then we will be killed by you for sure.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.110
We have two on this side.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.780
If you try anything funny, one of us will shoot you.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.110
Don't move!

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:16.990
Stop!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.530
Don't aim your gun at her.

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.620
Don't order me around!

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.420
Fine. This is going to last longer.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.710
Why?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.930
Why has it turned to this?

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.720
They're late. Too late.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.020
It's already been eight hours.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:49.060
Good grief. How far have those two gone on a recon?

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.020
Do you really think so?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.780
It's obviously too late.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.030
This means that those two are in...

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.650
We already know that.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.700
What will we do?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:02.120
When Commander is not around, you are in control.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.750
There's nothing else to do.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:06.870
We should go get...

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.500
This area is under enemy control.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.710
Just standing ground here is already dangerous.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.840
Are you saying that we should abandon them?

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.630
I will not stand for such a thing.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.760
Even if it means me alone...

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.970
Stop, Rosie.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.220
We will wait and see for the next two hours.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.100
I will make a judgment by then.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.310
Understood.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.570
Damn. Well, aren't you all lax.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.780
Those two are in trouble, you know.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.660
Hey, Darcsen. You hear me, right?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.200
Stop it, Rosie.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.370
Why should I?!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.200
The one who's most burdened is Isara.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.910
Don't pick on her now.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.540
Well then, why isn't she...

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:52.080
She has faith...

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.500
that Commander will make it back.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.590
Damn it.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.090
Welkin.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:06.220
You better not think of anything stupid!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:08.230
That's our line.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.810
Why are you doing something like this?

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:13.520
You probably came here to find shelter from the blizzard, but...

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.020
is there any meaning for holding out things like those?

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.280
Shut up!

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.440
We are stranded as well.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:20.860
Even if you didn't do anything like that...

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.070
Shut up!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.830
You're injured!

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.330
Don't move!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.170
Alicia!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.100
If we don't give you first aid...

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.390
Don't come any closer.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.470
Just sit down.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.560
But...

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:50.980
It's a warning.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.810
Sit at the count of five.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:55.270
Next time, I'll shoot you in the head.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.570
Five!

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.940
Stop or I will shoot you.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:00.900
Four!

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.910
If you do anything like that you'll die as well.

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.660
This is not a bluff.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.160
I mean it here as well.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.740
Sit down, right now.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.290
Three!

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:11.040
Alicia, sit down.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.750
You must not agitate him any further.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:13.920
Two!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:17.840
One!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.420
Stop it, already!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:23.260
Alicia?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.840
Giving you first aid is top priority.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.260
If you want to shoot me, do as you want.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.310
Stop!

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.390
But...

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.640
We are soldiers,

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.230
but before that, we are human beings.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:43.780
Show me your wound.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.620
Don't do anything funny.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.790
What's wrong?

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.250
If you're going to do it, make it fast.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.340
O-Okay.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.260
But do not forget.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.220
I have this in my hand.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.770
Damn it. Come back already.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.980
We don't have much time.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:17.810
Rosie.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:18.980
Something wrong?

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.020
It's nothing.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.570
I understand how you feel,

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.900
but how people deal with things are all different.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:30.450
There are those like you who have to say it when they think it,

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.000
and there those that have faith and just strive to get their things done.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.960
However, this one thing, everyone shares.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.800
Everyone is worried about Commander and Alicia.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.130
I understand that already.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:51.430
Damn it. This is making me look stupid.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.350
It's time.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.820
This doesn't look good. His face is pale.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:14.750
If he loses consciousness, the grenade will go off.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:18.040
Isn't there a way to save all of us?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.960
You, girl. Do you have some water?

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:22.710
I do.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:23.840
Hand it over.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.550
Throw it!

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.180
Going to shoot me again?

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:37.430
You...

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.270
Save your thanks for the owner of this cabin.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.110
It isn't mine.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.650
Go ahead, drink.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:56.910
Are you okay?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.620
Yes, no problem.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:59.750
Go.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.670
I'll leave the canteen here.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.260
Why did it turn out like this?

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.090
Is that wound from battle?

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:12.050
Huh?

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.680
Why do you ask of such a thing?

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.350
Let's just say that I got sick of holding my gun in silence.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.650
You're a pretty weird guy.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:23.150
I get that a lot.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.360
You two. You're militias?

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.110
Yes, that's right.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.490
As expected.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.910
But this is pretty ironic...

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:39.080
for enemies to run into each other in the depth of the mountain.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.330
I will... probably die.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.380
I know it. It's my body.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:58.770
I always thought I was going to die gracefully in the battlefield,

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.480
but to fall on a mountain like this...

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:03.270
You should stop speaking.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.150
No, please listen.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.230
This is something like a will.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:13.860
I was a third son of a farming family who lacked education and work.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:18.910
I am pretty sure you know it, but the Empire is that of those born into nobility.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.290
It is a world where everything is decided by birth,

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:28.590
but if you join the military and have the capability, you can climb the social ladder.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:36.010
I thought that a brighter future was open and that I can climb higher.

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:39.640
However, that was a mistake.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:43.940
When the war started, we were forced to fight.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.810
Killing a lot of enemies and letting a lot of friends die...

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:50.940
What's in it for me for going through all that?!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.450
What was I trying to get by killing so many people?

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.780
That's enough! Calm down!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:02.700
I was scared so much I couldn't stand it, so...

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.500
I ran away.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:11.000
This wounds are from a fellow soldier that shot me from the back when I ran.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:15.050
Then why didn't you surrender immediately?!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:21.510
I heard that when one surrenders to the Gallians, they are shot on the spot.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:24.310
Foolish! That story is...

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.150
Yeah. Ironic it is...

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.400
You're not the one to blame.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.940
The one to blame is this war!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.780
You, what's your name?

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.910
Alicia. Alicia Melchiott.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.490
And you?

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:44.620
Welkin Gunther.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.670
Is that so?

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:10.190
It should be okay now.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:13.440
Alicia, Welkin.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.190
It was nice to be able to talk with you two.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.370
Please listen to my last words.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:30.170
I was alive in this world.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:32.340
Please remember me.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:38.550
My name is Michael... Michael Weber.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.200
This way, sir!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.330
What is this?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.450
It seems like a grave.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.290
So, Michael has fallen.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.300
There are two footprints.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.760
From the bootprints, they seem to be from Gallian Soldiers.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.090
What will we do, sir?

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:22.970
If we chase them now, we will be able to catch them.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:24.890
No, there is no need for them.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:28.430
Even though he was a deserter, they paid respect to our fallen comrade.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:31.640
We are indebted to them.

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:36.900
Will everyone still be around?

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.490
It's been sixteen hours since we left the Squad.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.700
It would be normal for them to have retreated.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:46.790
Which means that we are not out of this trouble yet.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.540
I guess that's what it means.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:57.130
Well, our squad is not normal as expected.

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.510
Welkin!

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:01.130
Hooray!

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.590
Hey!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.010
We are back, everyone!

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:13.140
Little! Too little!

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:17.850
Why is there so little appearance for me, Edie Nelson?

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:24.160
Over a billion fans are waiting for my entrance!

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.950
Come out here, please, director!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:33.120
Next, on Valkyria Chronicles: Chapter Eleven - Uninvited Guests.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:39.410
A flower is noble and fragrant. Touch this flower, but beware its thorns.

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 11

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:40.000
Uninvited Guests
